  "Case reference: 2014003748": {
    "CaseRef": "Case reference: 2014003748",
    "CaseDesc": "On September 29, 1996, the police were contacted by a friend who reported that three of his hunting partners, including Glen Mymryk, had been missing from a hunting trip. The three men left in a loaded boat and reached halfway to their destination when they decided the water conditions were too challenging and they turned around. The men were bailing, but the waves were too much for them to handle. The motor stalled and they capsized. Glen was last seen floating away soon after the boat capsized. The sole survivor was rescued seven hours after the incident, at which point it was ascertained that the other two men had drowned.",
    "CaseType": "Missing",
    "CaseURL": "https://www.services.rcmp-grc.gc.ca/missing-disparus/case-dossier.jsf?case=2014003748&id=1&lang=en",
